  "assessments": {
    "legacy": "Compared the six 2.3.6 source sections covering feature minimum, AWS region list, external-model routing, base-service scope, the older installation and SAIA-9918. The legacy block and fallback apply to named app versions. The current release and installation pages supersede the prediction in that old issue.",
    "itsi": "The 2.3.6 and 2.4.0 overview sections independently name ITSI 5.0.0, MCP Server 1.2.1, and SAIA 2.2.0 as minima. Six ITSI tools are described. Reviewed base region and installation tables separately. Neither establishes a feature-specific regional rollout, user permission or exact app/Platform pairing.",
    "current": "The 2.4.0 Cloud compatibility table marks the app GA. The dedicated fresh Enterprise installer requires Enterprise 10.4+, SAIA 2.4.0+, Cloud Connect 2.0+, paid license, certificate and administrative setup, verified email, AWS selection and outbound HTTPS. The feature page still gives the wider 10.1.x floor. The release notes exclude Agent Mode from supported FedRAMP High core functionality. The 2.4.0 known-issues page retains a future-tense description. No tenant or generic newer combination was tested.",
    "region": "Compared all 15 named AWS Agent Mode locations against the feature table and distinct Model Runtime Data zone/Global and Azure rows. The four extra Azure labels identify only base service locations. Compared the ES Essentials, Premier and Cloud Connect tables row by row. Milan and São Paulo do not list the Security AI Assistant among their component exceptions. The Premier UAE row says AWS services disrupted. A Cloud Connect row for one named component cannot establish other agent rollouts. GovCloud component exceptions and GCP/Azure product-only rows remain separate from offering certification.",
    "soc": "Compared 8.8 Triage Premier Cloud/CMP and Autonomous Response Controlled Availability, Cloud-only cell versus CMP compatibility bullet, separate Cloud 8.6+ versus detailed 8.7+ minimums, CMP 10.4/8.8/2.0/2.4 floors, separate SOAR pairing and permissions. Checked 200 tenant analyses and 20 investigation revisions in parent against first-ten, approximately 200 findings and no rerun in task. The 8.7 task contains an older Cloud-only chain and frontier-model limits. Paid/representative enablement, endpoint region and customer authorization remain independent."
  },
